# Reachability-map request: solve a uniform grid of IK goals on a plane.
#
# The plane is described by its pose (position + orientation quaternion
# plane_orientation_*) and extents. grid_size_x cells span plane_size_x along
# the plane's local X axis and grid_size_y cells span plane_size_y along its
# local Y axis, centred on the pose. Every cell is solved with the exact plane
# orientation (positions vary, orientation is constant), which keeps the tool
# oriented the same at every grid point.
float64 plane_position_x
float64 plane_position_y
float64 plane_position_z
float64 plane_orientation_x
float64 plane_orientation_y
float64 plane_orientation_z
float64 plane_orientation_w
float64 plane_size_x
float64 plane_size_y
uint32 grid_size_x
uint32 grid_size_y

# TF frame the plane pose is expressed in; "" (or the robot base frame)
# means no transform is needed. The server resolves every other frame into
# the configured base link via TF before solving, and returns the solved
# grid (metrics.goals / metrics.plane_pose) in this same frame so a viewer
# can render it directly (SetMask.srv convention).
string frame_id ""
---
# Solver outcome. On a solver failure `success` is false, `message` explains,
# and `metrics.goals` still carries the requested grid (all cells marked
# unsolved) so a viewer can show geometry even on failure.
ReachabilityMetrics metrics
bool success
string message